  {
   "name": "d27-decision-receipt-inert",
   "why": "A decision receipt is a record with effects:{} carrying a gate verdict in reason. It must be STATE-INERT: SS5.2 iterates 'for each key K that R sets', so a record setting no key can never become a setter, create a conflict, or change state. This is the property that makes the receipt safe to write unconditionally, and it is a claim about the FOLD, not about one port. Also pins that a receipt's presence changes the topo ORDER (it is still a record in the set) while leaving state, setters and the conflict ledger byte-identical. NB: t1 sets owner=null and t2 sets owner=\"me\", so the ledger carries TWO conflicts. The receipt itself contributes neither: n1 sets no key, so it can never be a winner or a loser.",
   "records": [
    {
     "id": "t1",
     "kind": "task",
     "parents": [],
     "effects": {
      "status": "wip",
      "owner": null
     },
     "reason": "started"
    },
    {
     "id": "n1",
     "kind": "witness",
     "parents": [
      "t1"
     ],
     "effects": {},
     "reason": "gate:act should_apply=0.93 parent=t1-is-setter"
    },
    {
     "id": "t2",
     "kind": "task",
     "parents": [
      "n1"
     ],
     "effects": {
      "status": "done",
      "owner": "me"
     },
     "reason": "work complete"
    }
   ],
   "expect": {
    "state": {
     "status": "done",
     "owner": "me"
    },
    "setters": {
     "status": "t2",
     "owner": "t2"
    },
    "order": [
     "t1",
     "n1",
     "t2"
    ],
    "conflicts": [
     {
      "key": "owner",
      "winner": "t2",
      "losers": [
       "t1"
      ]
     },
     {
      "key": "status",
      "winner": "t2",
      "losers": [
       "t1"
      ]
     }
    ],
    "orphans": []
   }
  },
  {
   "name": "d28-licensed-action-applies",
   "why": "The receipt IS the parent of the action. With it present the action applies; without it (d29) the same action is an orphan and is excluded from state. Together the two cases are the cross-port proof that a decision structurally LICENCES an action -- you cannot hold the action without the record that licensed it, and that is a property of the FOLD, not of one port's receipt helper.",
